      "description": "Watch Stevenage vs Reading highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. Stevenage and Reading faced off in a highly anticipated Carabao Cup clash on August 25, 2026. Both sides entered the pitch with high hopes of advancing in the competition, setting the stage for an intense encounter. Early Dominance by the Royals The visitors established control early in the match, finding the breakthrough in just the 9th minute. Jacob Brown clinically dispatched a right-footed shot into the bottom corner after a well-placed cross from Paddy Lane . Stevenage attempted to fight back, with Jordan Roberts and Jack Taylor testing the resolve of Reading goalkeeper Joel Pereira , but the visitors remained resolute. Their persistence paid off again in the 24th minute when Paddy Lane turned from provider to scorer, firing a left-footed strike into the center of the goal to double the lead before the break. Second Half Pressure and Final Blow Seeking a way back into the contest, Stevenage made a triple substitution early in the second half, introducing Carl Piergianni , Michael Mellon , and Joe Knight . The home side showed more intent, and Phoenix Patterson forced a spectacular save from Joel Pereira at the top corner. Despite several corners and crosses from Dan Butler , the Stevenage attack could not find a way past a disciplined Reading backline. As the clock ticked down, Reading capitalized on the space left by the searching hosts. In the 85th minute, substitute Kyreece Lisbie set up Randell Williams , who finished from close range to make it 3-0. The match ended with some late friction as Benn Ward and Carl Piergianni both received yellow cards, but the result was beyond doubt as the Royals secured their progression in the tournament. Key Match Events 9' : Jacob Brown scores the opener assisted by Paddy Lane . 24' : Paddy Lane doubles the advantage with a clinical finish. 61' : Joel Pereira makes a vital save to deny Phoenix Patterson . 85' : Randell Williams seals the win from close range."
