      "description": "Watch Reading vs Luton highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The League One encounter between Reading and Luton on August 15, 2026 , delivered a spectacle that defied expectations, keeping the crowd on the edge of their seats until the very last second. Marriott's First-Half Masterclass The match ignited instantly, and Luton wasted no time in making their mark. Just 6 minutes in, Jake Richards found the back of the net following a sharp assist from Jordan Clark . However, the lead was short-lived as Jack Marriott took command of the game. The Reading striker leveled the score just two minutes later, sparking a remarkable individual performance. Marriott struck again in the 31st minute to put the hosts ahead and completed a stunning hat-trick by the 38th minute, assisted by Kyreece Lisbie , sending Reading into the break with a commanding 3-1 lead. The Luton Resurgence and Late Drama The second half saw a dramatic shift in momentum as Luton emerged with renewed intent. Kasey Palmer became the catalyst for the comeback, scoring twice in quick succession. He pulled one back in the 50th minute and, just three minutes later, latched onto a Nahki Wells assist to restore parity at 3-3. The contest grew increasingly physical, with Liam Walsh and Paudie O'Connor receiving yellow cards as both sides searched for a winner in the closing stages. Deep into stoppage time, the game reached its fever pitch. In the 96th minute, Gideon Kodua turned the match on its head, firing home the winning goal after being set up by Jake Richards . Although Kodua was booked for his celebration shortly after, his strike secured a breathtaking 4-3 victory for Luton , completing a comeback that will live long in the memory of the traveling supporters."
